class Solution {
    public int[] pivotArray(int[] nums, int pivot) {
        List<Integer> less = new ArrayList<>();
        List<Integer> equal = new ArrayList<>();
        List<Integer> greater = new ArrayList<>();

        // Step 1: Partition elements into three lists
        for (int num: nums){
            if(num<pivot){
                less.add(num);
            }else if(num==pivot){
                equal.add(num);
            }else{
                greater.add(num);
            }
        }

        // Step 2: Concatenate results
        int[] result = new int[nums.length];
        int index=0;
        for (int num: less) result[index++] = num;
        for (int num: equal) result[index++] = num;
        for (int num: greater) result[index++] = num;
        return result;
    }
}


Time Complexity: O(n) (single pass through array).
Space Complexity: O(n) (three lists + result array).

Method2: WITH O(1) space
class Solution {
    public int[] pivotArray(int[] nums, int pivot) {
        int n = nums.length;
        
        // Step 1: Count how many elements are less, equal, greater
        int lessCount = 0, equalCount = 0;
        for(int num : nums){
            if(num < pivot) lessCount++;
            else if(num == pivot) equalCount++;
        }
        
        // Step 2: Compute starting indices for each section
        int lessIndex = 0;
        int equalIndex = lessCount;
        int greaterIndex = lessCount + equalCount;
        
        // Step 3: Create result array
        int[] result = new int[n];
        
        // Step 4: Place elements directly into correct section
        for(int num : nums){
            if(num < pivot){
                result[lessIndex++] = num;
            }else if(num == pivot){
                result[equalIndex++] = num;
            }else{
                result[greaterIndex++] = num;
            }
        }
        return result;
    }
}

Time Complexity: O(n) (single pass to count, single pass to place).
Space Complexity: O(1) extra (only counters and pointers; output array is required anyway).
